      en: "The Tomb of King Koffi is located in Abomey, the historic center of the Kingdom of Dahomey. King Koffi (also known as Kpengla) reigned in the 18th century and was known for his military campaigns. The tomb is part of the Royal Palaces of Abomey, a UNESCO World Heritage site. It is a traditional mud structure with elaborate decorations. The tomb serves as an important memorial for descendants of the Dahomey dynasty.",
