      en: "The Palace of the King of Allada, located in Allada, southern Benin, was the political and religious center of the Kingdom of Allada, which flourished from the 15th to the 18th centuries. The palace compound features multiple courtyards, a throne room, and sacred groves. Its architecture incorporates both traditional mud-brick and influences from early European traders. The palace remains a symbol of royal authority and hosts the annual Gaani festival. It was declared a national monument in 1964.",
